cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the article and identify the commit used."
type: software
title: "Nonhalting and PA-unprovability for a 213-state Turing machine"
authors:
  - family-names: "Chang"
    given-names: "James"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jamesyc/BusyBeaver"
abstract: >-
  Assuming the consistency of ordinary Peano arithmetic, an explicit binary
  Turing machine with 213 working states runs forever on a blank tape and PA
  cannot prove its nonhalting sentence. The Lean formalization checks the
  machine simulation and the internal implication from nonhalting to PA consistency.
